# Retained ARM64 exception-table coverage: staged proposal

This static diagnostic expands B6.4's compiled-path coverage across the two
retained standalone worker images. It reads compact-unwind metadata and Rust
LSDA tables, then follows ordinary control from both function entries and all
table-listed landing pads of reached owners. It never executes a worker or
changes the Rust implementation, resource contract, historical evidence or
production gate.

The result is **conditional metadata and control coverage**, not an exception
semantics proof, panic-freedom argument, termination proof or resource bound.
Every complete native, stack, workspace, physical-calibration and qualification
flag remains false. The selected images remain historical: the later checkout
and dependency graph do not inherit their build or observation results.

